// BL-1 adversarial: unit/void values used as control-flow heads (the
// condition / iterable / subject positions feed codegen helpers that used to
// `?.unwrap()` the compiled subexpression). Parseable; sema rejects them with
// a clean diagnostic and a non-zero (non-101) exit — never a panic.
fn main() {
    if print(0) {
        print(1)
    }
    for x in print(0) {
        print(x)
    }
    match print(0) {
        _ => print(1)
    }
}
